{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebAlgebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebAlgebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.FreeAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.RingQuot","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Idempotent","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":57,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_int_one_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_int_one_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":602,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L602-L615","doc":"**The two generators of `TL₃(1)` over `ℤ` are nonzero and distinct.** An\nunconditional instance of `tl3_adjacent_nondegenerate`, at `δ = c = 1`, where the two\nmatrix generators are `!![1,0;0,0]` and `!![1,1;0,0]`.\n\nNote that `δ = 1` satisfies `δ² = 1`, so the two nonzero-ness conjuncts are exactly the\nones a commutative model would also give (module docstring, §*Non-vacuity*). The final\nconjunct `e₀ ≠ e₁` is the one that is unavailable commutatively, and it is what makes\nthis an unconditional witness with content rather than a restatement of `nontrivial`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2_int_two_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2_int_two_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":595,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L595-L600","doc":"**`TL₂(2)` over `ℤ` has `1` and `e` linearly independent.** An unconditional\ninstance of `tl2_linearIndependent`: `2` is a non-zero-divisor in `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_adjacent_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_adjacent_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L576-L584","doc":"**The adjacency relation is non-vacuous in `TL₃(δ)`**: it holds, and the two\ngenerators it relates are nonzero and distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_e_zero_ne_e_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_e_zero_ne_e_one","kind":"theorem","line":558,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L558-L574","doc":"**The two generators of `TL₃(δ)` are distinct.** Their images differ in the `(0,1)`\nentry — `0` for `M₀` against the unit `c` for `M₁`.\n\nThis is the one statement in this section that a commutative model cannot supply: the\nrelations force `e₀ = e₁` in any commutative algebra (module docstring), whereas\nnonzero-ness of each generator separately is available commutatively whenever\n`δ² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_e_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_e_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":545,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L545-L556","doc":"**The second generator of `TL₃(δ)` is nonzero.** Its image has `(0,0)` entry\n`c = δ⁻¹`, which is a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_e_zero_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3_e_zero_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":532,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L532-L543","doc":"**The first generator of `TL₃(δ)` is nonzero.** Its image has `(0,0)` entry `δ`,\nwhich is a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Rep_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Rep_e","kind":"theorem","line":528,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L528-L530","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Rep","kind":"def","line":523,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L523-L526","doc":"**The two-generator matrix representation of `TL₃(δ)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_comm","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L513-L521","doc":"**The matrix family satisfies the commutation relation**, which for two generators\nfires only at `i = j` and is then trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":504,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L504-L511","doc":"**The matrix family satisfies the adjacency relation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_sq","kind":"theorem","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L496-L502","doc":"**The matrix family satisfies the loop relation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₁₀₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₁₀₁","kind":"theorem","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L486-L494","doc":"`M₁ M₀ M₁ = M₁`, using `c δ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₀₁₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₀₁₀","kind":"theorem","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L478-L484","doc":"`M₀ M₁ M₀ = M₀`, using `c δ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₁_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₁_sq","kind":"theorem","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L470-L476","doc":"`M₁² = δ M₁`. This one needs no hypothesis on `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₀_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₀_sq","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L462-L468","doc":"`M₀² = δ M₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_one","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L460-L460","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam_zero","kind":"theorem","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L458-L458","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3Fam","kind":"def","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L455-L456","doc":"The two matrices, as a family indexed by the two generators of `TL₃(δ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₁","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L451-L453","doc":"Second matrix generator: `δ` times a rank-one idempotent whose triple product with\nthe first collapses by exactly `δ⁻²`. Here `c` plays the role of `δ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl3M₀","kind":"def","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L448-L449","doc":"First matrix generator: `δ` times the rank-one idempotent `diag(1,0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2e_ne_algebraMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2e_ne_algebraMap","kind":"theorem","line":418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L418-L427","doc":"**The generator of `TL₂(δ)` is not a scalar** when the loop parameter is a\nnon-zero-divisor over a nontrivial ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L393-L416","doc":"**`1` and `e` are `R`-linearly independent in `TL₂(δ)`** whenever the loop\nparameter is a non-zero-divisor.\n\nThis is the non-vacuity statement with content: the presentation does not secretly\nidentify the generator with a scalar. It is the **lower-bound half** of the classical\n\"`TL₂(δ)` is free of rank two on `{1, e}`\" — this file proves no upper bound on\n`TL₂(δ)`, so freeness itself is not claimed here.\n\n**The other half is now proved** in\n`QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebSpanning`: `tl2_span_eq_top` supplies the upper\nbound and `tl2Basis` assembles the two into a `Module.Basis (Fin 2)`. So the\nclassical statement holds; it simply is not established in this file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2e_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2e_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L385-L391","doc":"**The generator of `TL₂(δ)` is nonzero** whenever the loop parameter is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2Rep_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2Rep_e","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L380-L381","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2Rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2Rep","kind":"def","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L370-L378","doc":"**The representation `TL₂(δ) → R × R`, `e ↦ (δ, 0)`.**\n\nThe loop relation is `(δ,0)² = (δ²,0) = (δ,δ)·(δ,0)`; the adjacency relation never\nfires because `Fin 1` has no adjacent pair; and `R × R` is commutative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.tl2e","kind":"def","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L367-L368","doc":"The unique generator of `TL₂(δ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.TL2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.TL2","kind":"def","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L364-L365","doc":"`TL₂(δ)`: the Temperley–Lieb algebra on one generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_commute_fin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_commute_fin","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L329-L336","doc":"`e_i e_j = e_j e_i` when `|i − j| ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_adjacent_fin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_adjacent_fin","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L322-L327","doc":"`e_i e_j e_i = e_i` when `|i − j| = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_sq_fin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_sq_fin","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L316-L320","doc":"`e_i² = δ e_i` in `TL_{n+1}(δ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.TLFin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.TLFin","kind":"def","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L311-L314","doc":"**The classical Temperley–Lieb algebra `TL_{n+1}(δ)`**: `n` generators\n`e_0, …, e_{n-1}` — the literature's `e_1, …, e_n` — on `n + 1` strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.not_adjFin_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.not_adjFin_one","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L303-L309","doc":"`Fin 1` carries no adjacent pair, so `TL₂(δ)` has a single unconstrained\ngenerator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.adjFin_irrefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.adjFin_irrefl","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L299-L301","doc":"Adjacency on `Fin n` is irreflexive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.adjFin_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.adjFin_symm","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L296-L297","doc":"Adjacency on `Fin n` is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.instDecidableAdjFin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.instDecidableAdjFin","kind":"instance","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L293-L294","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.adjFin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.adjFin","kind":"def","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L290-L291","doc":"Adjacency on `Fin n`: `i` and `j` are adjacent when `|i − j| = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L274-L282","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb algebra does not collapse.** Over a nontrivial base ring,\n`0 ≠ 1` in `TemperleyLiebAlgebra R δ Adj`.\n\nWithout this, every theorem in this file would be vacuously true of the zero ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.augmentation_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.augmentation_e","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L271-L272","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.augmentation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.augmentation","kind":"def","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L266-L269","doc":"**The augmentation** `e_i ↦ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.exists_unique_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.exists_unique_lift","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L250-L258","doc":"**The universal property**, as a single `∃!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.hom_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.hom_ext","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L231-L248","doc":"**Uniqueness.** Two `R`-algebra maps out of the Temperley–Lieb algebra agreeing on\nevery generator are equal.\n\n`RingQuot.mkAlgHom` is surjective, so it suffices that the composites agree; those are\nmaps out of a *free* algebra, so `FreeAlgebra.hom_ext` reduces that to the\ngenerators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.lift_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.lift_e","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L222-L229","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.lift","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L205-L220","doc":"**Existence.** A family `f : B → A` satisfying the three relations induces an\n`R`-algebra map out of the Temperley–Lieb algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.isIdempotentElem_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.isIdempotentElem_e","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L195-L199","doc":"**The rescaled generator is idempotent.** For `c` inverse to the loop parameter,\n`c · e_i` squares to itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.isIdempotentElem_smul_of_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.isIdempotentElem_smul_of_sq","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L177-L193","doc":"**Rescaling a `δ`-quadratic element makes it idempotent.**\n\nIf `a * a = d * a` in an `R`-algebra and `c * d = 1` in `R`, then `c * a` is\nidempotent. Stated for an arbitrary algebra element, since nothing about the\nTemperley–Lieb presentation is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.commute_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.commute_e","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L165-L168","doc":"The commutation relation in the `Commute` form Mathlib's API expects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_farCommute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_farCommute","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L159-L163","doc":"**Non-adjacent generators commute.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L153-L157","doc":"**The adjacency relation holds.** `e_i e_j e_i = e_i` for adjacent `i, j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e_sq","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L146-L151","doc":"**The loop relation holds.** `e_i² = δ e_i` in the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.e","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L140-L142","doc":"The generator `e_i`, the image of the free generator `i` in the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.instAlgebraTemperleyLiebAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.instAlgebraTemperleyLiebAlgebra","kind":"instance","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L137-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.instRingTemperleyLiebAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.instRingTemperleyLiebAlgebra","kind":"instance","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L134-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.TemperleyLiebAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.TemperleyLiebAlgebra","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L130-L132","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb algebra** on the index type `B` with adjacency `Adj`, over\n`R`, at loop parameter `δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.Rel.farCommute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.Rel.farCommute","kind":"ctor","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L125-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.Rel.adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.Rel.adjacent","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L123-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.Rel.sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.Rel.sq","kind":"ctor","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L120-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.Rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLieb.Rel","kind":"inductive","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebAlgebra.lean#L112-L126","doc":"The three defining families of the Temperley–Lieb algebra, as a relation on the\nfree algebra: the **loop** relation `e_i² = δ e_i` for each generator, the\n**adjacency** relation `e_i e_j e_i = e_i` for each adjacent ordered pair, and\n**commutation** of each non-adjacent pair.\n\n`RingQuot` closes this up into a ring congruence, so listing the raw relations here is\nenough — there is no ideal to generate and no two-sided-span reasoning downstream. ","signatureChunk":0}]}